+# MyNest Unified Marketplace v3.13.53
+
+## Seller-authenticated REST hardening (mobile "wpcomsh-fatal" repro)
+
+Mobile screenshot from 2026-08-31 showed the raw WordPress.com `.wpcomsh-fatal`
+CSS ruleset rendered inside the Payout bank account screen. On WordPress.com /
+Pressable / Atomic hosts, an unhandled PHP fatal returns the wpcomsh
+"Something went wrong" HTML/CSS template — which the mobile app then displayed
+verbatim in an inline error card (not a toast, so the toast-boundary sanitizer
+did not catch it).
+
+This release wraps every seller-authenticated REST callback most likely to
+fatal with a `\Throwable` boundary. On failure, the callback:
+
+- Logs the underlying diagnostic to `error_log` for admins
+- Returns a structured JSON `WP_Error` with HTTP 500 and a plain-English message
+- Never returns HTML/CSS to the client
+
+### Hardened endpoints
+
+| Endpoint | File | Function |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `GET /the-nest/v1/seller/bank-account` | `class-mnu-bank-account.php` | `rest_get` |
+| `POST /the-nest/v1/seller/bank-account` | `class-mnu-bank-account.php` | `rest_save` (delegates to `rest_save_impl`) |
+| `GET /the-nest/v1/seller/readiness` | `class-mnu-seller-readiness.php` | `rest_readiness` |
+| `GET /the-nest/v1/seller/earnings` | `class-tnm-rest.php` | `seller_earnings` |
+| `GET /the-nest/v1/seller/payouts` | `class-tnm-rest.php` | `seller_payouts` |
+| `POST /the-nest/v1/seller/payouts` | `class-tnm-rest.php` | `seller_payout_request` |
+
+### Return-type additions
+
+`seller_earnings` and `seller_payouts` now declare `WP_REST_Response|WP_Error`
+so the JSON error path is valid without loosening the return signature.
+
+### What it does NOT change
+
+- Payment creation, checkout finalization, tax calculation, refunds, or
+  seller-payout batching contracts.
+- The v3.13.52 seller-application boundary (that fix is still in place).
+- Any client-visible response schema when the endpoint succeeds.
+
+### Paired mobile change (v1.0.174)
+
+Mobile client now sanitizes server dumps at the `ApiError.friendly`
+construction site so every screen — not just the toast host — is safe from
+raw HTML/CSS output.
